---
import SectionPageHeader from
  "../components/SectionPageHeader.astro";

import SiteLayout from
  "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Acknowledgements"
  description="Credits, licensing, privacy information, and disclaimers for Fabrizio's Webhome."
  lang="en"
  contentClass="acknowledgements-main"
>
  <SectionPageHeader
    title="Acknowledgements"
    subtitle="About This Site"
    introduction={`Credits, sources, terms of reuse,
and a few necessary caveats.`}
  />

  <article class="information-page">
    <section
      class="information-page__section information-page__section--wide"
      aria-labelledby="about-this-webhome"
    >
      <h2 id="about-this-webhome">
        About this Webhome
      </h2>

      <p>
        Fabrizio’s Webhome is a personal and evolving
        collection of projects, thoughts, experiments,
        games, and other artifacts by Fabrizio Caragiulo.
        It was conceived as a place in which unfinished
        processes may remain visible alongside completed
        work.
      </p>

      <p>
        The site was designed and developed iteratively
        by Fabrizio Caragiulo with assistance from
        OpenAI Codex. Editorial decisions, published
        materials, and final responsibility for the
        site remain Fabrizio’s.
      </p>

      <p>
        The website is built with
        {" "}
        <a href="https://astro.build/">
          Astro
        </a>,
        TypeScript, HTML, and CSS. Font files are
        self-hosted, partly through
        {" "}
        <a href="https://fontsource.org/">
          Fontsource
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="information-page__section information-page__section--wide" aria-labelledby="credits">
      <h2 id="credits">Credits</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Fonts:</strong> <a href="https://velvetyne.fr/fonts/basteleur/">Basteleur</a> by Keussel / Velvetyne; <a href="https://github.com/huertatipografica/Alegreya">Alegreya</a> by the Alegreya Project Authors; <a href="https://github.com/productiontype/Spectral">Spectral</a> by Production Type; <a href="https://github.com/arrowtype/recursive">Recursive</a> by the Recursive Project Authors; Prosto One by Jovanny Lemonad and Pavel Emelyanov. Fonts are self-hosted and retain their respective licences.</li>
        <li><strong>Photographs and lettering:</strong> header photographs by Fabrizio Caragiulo and E. N.; the courtyard photograph in <i>Cervi Units</i> provided by M. d.C.; handwritten wordmark by Fabrizio Caragiulo.</li>
        <li><strong>Crow:</strong> from <a href="https://peakpixels.itch.io/commonbirds">Common Birds</a> by Peak Pixels, purchased and used under its author’s terms.</li>
        <li><strong>Tiles:</strong> pixel-art adaptations by Fabrizio Caragiulo of <a href="https://wordpress.org/photos/photo/4636317663/">Marco Almeida / Webdados’s photograph of Lisbon tile magnets</a>, available through the WordPress Photo Directory under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/">CC0</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Corner ornament:</strong> adapted by Fabrizio Caragiulo from G. A. and M. A. Audsley’s <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vintage_pattern_from_The_Practical_Decorator_and_Ornamentist_by_G.A_%26_M.A._Audsley_from_rawpixel%E2%80%99s_own_original_first_edition_of_the_publication_67.jpg">The Practical Decorator and Ornamentist</a>, digitised by Rawpixel. Source and adaptation: <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Family tree:</strong> the chart in <i>Caragiulorigin</i> was generated with <a href="https://www.familysearch.org/">FamilySearch</a> using genealogical research by Fabrizio Caragiulo.</li>
        <li><strong>Spinning cow:</strong> GIF hosted by <a href="https://onlinewahn.de/kuh24.gif">Onlinewahn</a>; original creator not yet identified. I thank Sasha for letting me know this gem.</li>
        <li><strong>Translations:</strong> original authors and source texts are credited on the individual pages.</li>
        <li><strong>Playlist images:</strong> edited versions of third-party thumbnails, video stills and artwork, accompanied by links to the associated videos. Rights in the underlying images remain with their respective rightsholders.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="information-page__section information-page__section--wide" aria-labelledby="licensing">
      <h2 id="licensing">Reuse &amp; privacy</h2>
      <p>Unless otherwise noted, my original writings, games and graphics are shared under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Site-specific code is available under the <a href="https://opensource.org/license/mit">MIT licence</a>.</p>
      <p>Photographs, translations, playlist images, the CV, personal information, the FamilySearch chart and third-party assets are excluded from that general content licence. Separate licences and rights remain applicable. Photographs by E. N. and M. d.C. are used with permission.</p>
      <p>For credit corrections or requests to remove third-party material, please <a href="mailto:fabrizio.caragiulo@gmail.com">email me</a>, identifying the page and material concerned.</p>
      <p>The site itself uses no analytics or advertising trackers. Browser storage remembers game progress and temporary interface settings. Some external images are loaded from third-party websites, which receive the corresponding requests. Hosting and external services have their own privacy policies.</p>
      <p>© 2026 Fabrizio Caragiulo.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
